WEBVTT

00:00:01.50 --> 00:00:03.61
Part seven planned the backlog.

00:00:03.61 --> 00:00:06.07
Part eight is stage ten, increments.

00:00:06.07 --> 00:00:11.86
Hewn now builds each increment test first, implements it until a fixed gate is green,

00:00:11.86 --> 00:00:17.38
records a video, opens a pull request, and squash-merges it once its checks pass,

00:00:17.38 --> 00:00:18.95
with no human approval.

00:00:20.10 --> 00:00:25.03
Stage ten asks the API for the next runnable increment, again and again,

00:00:25.03 --> 00:00:26.34
until none is left.

00:00:26.34 --> 00:00:31.00
Each increment gets a feature branch from the latest default branch.

00:00:31.00 --> 00:00:34.08
The first commit holds only acceptance tests,

00:00:34.08 --> 00:00:39.15
each tracing to the increment's requirements, and the red run is recorded.

00:00:39.50 --> 00:00:42.18
Then the agent implements in iterations.

00:00:42.18 --> 00:00:47.47
Each iteration ends with the gate: backend tests, frontend lint and unit tests,

00:00:47.47 --> 00:00:49.14
and the end to end suite.

00:00:49.14 --> 00:00:54.36
After ten failing iterations, the increment is blocked with its failing tests,

00:00:54.36 --> 00:00:58.85
and work moves on to the next increment that does not depend on it.

00:01:00.00 --> 00:01:03.06
The worker still holds no GitHub credential.

00:01:03.06 --> 00:01:06.61
Stage ten may commit code only to feature branches,

00:01:06.61 --> 00:01:09.39
and only progress to the default branch.

00:01:09.39 --> 00:01:15.23
It may open and merge only its own pull requests, and never touch branch protection.

00:01:15.58 --> 00:01:20.32
If the default branch moved, the merge is refused as branch behind.

00:01:20.32 --> 00:01:24.08
The worker replays its changes onto a fresh checkout,

00:01:24.08 --> 00:01:27.40
the agent resolves any file both sides changed,

00:01:27.40 --> 00:01:30.73
and the API moves the branch onto the new head.

00:01:30.73 --> 00:01:33.84
After three tries, the increment is blocked.

00:01:34.99 --> 00:01:40.07
The pull request is titled after the journey, with its requirement IDs.

00:01:40.07 --> 00:01:44.28
Its body has six sections: what, design and decisions, API,

00:01:44.28 --> 00:01:48.50
tests with each command's pass counts, deferred, and notes,

00:01:48.50 --> 00:01:51.57
and it ends with the Hewn attribution line.

00:01:51.92 --> 00:01:54.84
A failed check counts as a failed iteration.

00:01:54.84 --> 00:02:00.35
A video that fails twice is noted in the pull request and never holds the increment

00:02:00.35 --> 00:02:00.68
back.

00:02:00.68 --> 00:02:05.86
After each merge, the merged designs are marked complete and the estimates are

00:02:05.86 --> 00:02:08.71
committed before the next increment starts.

00:02:09.86 --> 00:02:15.18
The backend gained twenty tests: the backlog cursor, blocking, red and early green,

00:02:15.18 --> 00:02:19.98
the branch and path rules, merging with branch deletion, and branch behind.

00:02:19.98 --> 00:02:25.24
The worker gained twenty one, covering the guard, the gate, the pull request body,

00:02:25.24 --> 00:02:28.50
the video check, progress, and every executor path,

00:02:28.50 --> 00:02:30.62
from block to rebase to conflict.

00:02:31.77 --> 00:02:34.40
Here is the real app with one worker.

00:02:34.40 --> 00:02:35.68
The Owner submits.

00:02:35.68 --> 00:02:41.29
Stages zero to nine run, then stage ten takes each increment through its tests,

00:02:41.29 --> 00:02:46.34
iterations, video, pull request and merge, and the direction completes.

00:02:47.49 --> 00:02:53.06
Each increment now ships test first, through a green gate and a merged pull request,

00:02:53.06 --> 00:02:56.58
and the project's progress updates after every merge.

00:02:56.58 --> 00:03:01.95
Next, the last part of journey one: recorded decisions and the no approval end to

00:03:01.95 --> 00:03:02.55
end test.
